     "verdict": "pass",
     "content": "```python\nfrom collections import OrderedDict\n\nclass LRUCache:\n    def __init__(self, capacity: int):\n        self.capacity = capacity\n        self.cache = OrderedDict()\n\n    def get(self, key):\n        if key not in self.cache:\n            return -1\n        self.cache.move_to_end(key)\n        return self.cache[key]\n\n    def put(self, key, value):\n        if key in self.cache:\n            self.cache.move_to_end(key)\n        self.cache[key] = value\n        if len(self.cache) > self.capacity:\n            self.cache.popitem(last=False)\n```\n\nBoth `get` and `put` run in **O(1)** average time thanks to `OrderedDict`'s hash-based lookups and doubly-linked list for ordering."
    },
    {
     "verdict": "pass",
     "content": "```python\nfrom collections import OrderedDict\n\nclass LRUCache:\n    def __init__(self, capacity: int):\n        self.capacity = capacity\n        self.cache = OrderedDict()\n\n    def get(self, key):\n        if key not in self.cache:\n            return -1\n        self.cache.move_to_end(key)\n        return self.cache[key]\n\n    def put(self, key, value):\n        if key in self.cache:\n            self.cache.move_to_end(key)\n        self.cache[key] = value\n        if len(self.cache) > self.capacity:\n            self.cache.popitem(last=False)\n```\n\nBoth `get` and `put` run in **O(1)** average time, since `OrderedDict` provides constant-time lookups, insertions, and moves to either end."
